# Intelligent Tutoring Systems: Exploring Issues in Learning and Teaching Writing.

**Authors:** Neuwirth, Christine M.

## Abstract
Discusses the potential and the limitations of intelligent tutoring systems (ITS) in the teaching of writing. Outlines the goals and significance of research, and analyzes the pedagogical assumptions underlying such research. Describes the architecture of these systems and illustrates instructional design issues by describing the ITS program, PARNASSUS. (Author/LS)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ391407

